BOARD OVERVIEW
Your board consists of:

ESP32 microcontroller

AXS15231B 320x480 LCD display (QSPI interface)

Capacitive touch panel (I2C interface)

Backlight control pin

The ESP32 controls both the display and the touch panel.

––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––
DISPLAY (AXS15231B LCD DRIVER)
Interface: QSPI (Quad SPI)
Resolution: 320 x 480
Color: 16-bit RGB565

DISPLAY → ESP32 PIN MAP
QSPI_CS  -> GPIO 45
QSPI_SCK -> GPIO 47
QSPI_D0  -> GPIO 21
QSPI_D1  -> GPIO 48
QSPI_D2  -> GPIO 40
QSPI_D3  -> GPIO 39
TFT_BL   -> GPIO 1 (Backlight ON/OFF)

DISPLAY INITIALISATION (CONCEPT)

Use Arduino_GFX_Library

Create QSPI bus

Create AXS15231B display object

Begin display

Set rotation

Turn on backlight

DRAWING TEXT (CONCEPT)

Set text color

Set text size

Set cursor position

Print text

––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––
TOUCH PANEL (CAPACITIVE, I2C)
Interface: I2C
Touch controller address: 0x3B

TOUCH → ESP32 PIN MAP
SDA  -> GPIO 4
SCL  -> GPIO 8
INT  -> GPIO 3
RST  -> GPIO 38

TOUCH INITIALISATION (CONCEPT)

Begin I2C with SDA=4, SCL=8

Reset touch controller using GPIO 38

READING TOUCH (CONCEPT)

Send special 11-byte command to address 0x3B

Read 8 bytes of touch data

Extract X and Y coordinates

Rotate coordinates because screen is mounted upside-down

Return true if touch detected

––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––
BACKLIGHT CONTROL
Pin: GPIO 1
HIGH = backlight on
LOW = backlight off

